{# ============================================================================
   WATCHES — the four columns the roster owns on a station, ported from the
   design's configure.html#watches.

   THE NAME, KIND, POINT AND CALL SIGN ARE THE AREA'S. This section edits only
   what the roster owns: the shifts a post expects, how long its silence may
   run, how long before that is offline, and how wide its catchment is. Ruled
   18 sep, and it is why the rows here are read-only about everything else.

   ONE PLACE IT IS EDITED, TWO DOORS ONTO IT. The same block renders on the
   area's own Stations configure card; both call StationWatchService, and
   neither screen owns the other.

   A POST WITH NO WATCH IS NOT A FAULT. A post that declares none is never
   counted, never late and never a hole — only offline.

   AND A POST OFF THE BOOKS IS NOT INVISIBLE. The area's other posts are the
   add row's own list, so the section that says which posts this module
   works is also the one place a post joins them. Ported from the design's
   `.staddrow` on this card.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/configure/_frame.html.twig' %}

{% block roster_section %}
<form method="post" action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::SAVE_WATCHES_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
    <div class="c rband">
        {# HEADER = IDENTITY ONLY. Ruled 2026-09-20, measured against the
           area's own Stations configure card: a configure card's band says
           what the card IS and carries no door. Ways out are the section
           strip, the lit Configure action and the crumb. #}
        <div class="rb-hd">
            <span class="tab">Watches</span>
            <span class="rb-ttl">what each post expects, how long its silence may run, and how wide its catchment is</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rb-body">
            {% for watch in watches %}
                {% set station = watch.station %}
                {% set id = station.id %}
                <div class="rset">
                    <span class="lb"><b>{{ station.name }}</b><em>{{ station.code ?: '—' }}</em></span>
                    <span class="ct">
                        {% for shift in shifts %}
                            <label class="r-sh {{ shift.key in watch.expects ? 'on' : '' }}">
                                <input type="checkbox" name="expects_{{ id }}[]" value="{{ shift.key }}"
                                       {{ shift.key in watch.expects ? 'checked' : '' }}
                                       {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                                <i></i>{{ shift.label|lower }}
                            </label>
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="r-sh">no shift vocabulary</span>
                        {% endfor %}
                        {% if watch.expectsNothing %}<span class="r-sh">no watch</span>{% endif %}
                    </span>
                    <span class="why">
                        <span class="unit">silence</span>
                        <input class="fld" type="number" min="1" name="silence_{{ id }}" value="{{ watch.silenceWindowMinutes }}" aria-label="Silence window for {{ station.name }}, minutes" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                        <span class="unit">min, offline after</span>
                        <input class="fld" type="number" min="1" name="offline_{{ id }}" value="{{ watch.offlineAfterMinutes }}" aria-label="Offline threshold for {{ station.name }}, minutes" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                        <span class="unit">min, catchment</span>
                        <input class="fld" type="number" min="1" name="catchment_{{ id }}" value="{{ station.catchmentM ?? settings.defaultCatchmentMetres }}" aria-label="Catchment for {{ station.name }}, metres" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                        <span class="unit">m</span>
                        <span class="unit">pool {{ pools[id]|default(0) }}</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
            {% else %}
                <div class="rfrag"><b>No post is on the roster&rsquo;s books yet</b><em>the area registers {{ band.stationsInArea }} station{{ band.stationsInArea == 1 ? '' : 's' }}; a watch is given to a post deliberately, so none is assumed</em></div>
            {% endfor %}

            {# THE DOOR, AND IT IS THE REASON THIS SECTION EXISTS. Ported
               from the design's own `.staddrow` on this card: the add
               control on the left, the save at the right-hand end.

               ONE FORM, TWO SUBMITS. Adding a post and saving the page are
               two writes at two addresses, and `formaction` is how one form
               offers both — a second `<form>` cannot be nested inside this
               one, and a form outside it could not carry the same token.

               THE PICKER IS THIS MODULE'S ADDITION TO THE DRAWING, stated
               rather than slipped in: the design's button names no post
               because the drawing has one meaning and a running area has
               twelve, and a button that cannot say which post is not a
               control. It wears the reference card's own add-row shape —
               label, control, quiet button. #}
            {% if mayManage %}
                <div class="staddrow">
                    {% if postsOffTheBooks is not empty %}
                        <label class="fldlab" for="roster-add-post">Add a post</label>
                        <select class="fld" id="roster-add-post" name="station">
                            {% for station in postsOffTheBooks %}
                                <option value="{{ station.uuidString }}">{{ station.name }}{% if station.code %} &middot; {{ station.code }}{% endif %}</option>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </select>
                        <button type="submit" class="btn sm"
                                formaction="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::ADD_TO_ROSTER_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">Add a post to the roster</button>
                    {% else %}
                        <span class="more">every post this area registers is on these books</span>
                    {% endif %}
                    <span class="sp"></span>
                    <button type="submit" class="cta">Save the watches</button>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
</form>
{% endblock %}
